---

Collection data (data/manifest.json, data/scores.json, data/curate.json,
data/overrides.json, data/withheld-works.json): to the extent the selection,
arrangement, scores and one-line captions in these files are protectable at
all, they are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0
<https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/>. The metadata they
aggregate comes from CC0 sources (The Metropolitan Museum of Art, the Art
Institute of Chicago, the Cleveland Museum of Art, the National Gallery of
Art, Wikidata, and the Rijksmuseum's CC0 data) and from the licence and source
records of Wikimedia Commons.

---

Artwork images are downloaded by the app from their hosts. Each work is in
the public domain, or released under CC0 by the institution that holds it;
the evidence for each work, with a link to its source, is
recorded in data/manifest.json. Museum and collection names and marks belong
to their owners and are used only to identify the source of an image. Their
use does not imply endorsement of artbip.

---

Notes on works, artists, and periods and schools (the text in
data/education/starter.json, and any other file of such notes) are
(c) 2026 Alexander McGinn. All rights reserved. They may be read and displayed
within artbip, including copies of artbip built from this source code, but may
not otherwise be copied, republished or redistributed separately from artbip
without permission. The CC0 dedication above covers only the files it names
(including the one-line captions in data/manifest.json), not these notes.

The name "artbip" and the artbip icon are not licensed under any of the
above.
